data.content:
Modify the headers created to follow this standard:

A standard `manifest.json` block for a Thunderbird WebExtension requires `manifest_version: 2` (or `3` for later versions like 128+) and the `messagesRead` permission if you are modifying the header, or `compose` if it is an outgoing header add-on. [[1](https://webextension-api.thunderbird.net/), [2](https://webextension-api.thunderbird.net/en/mv3/compose.html), [3](https://webextension-api.thunderbird.net/en/esr-mv3/compose.html), [4](https://www.reddit.com/r/Thunderbird/comments/1srso7i/signed_thunderbird_extension_cli_that_exposes/)]
Here is the structured template for your `manifest.json` header extension:

json

```
{
  "manifest_version": 2,
  "manifest_version": 3, 
  "name": "Your Add-On Name",
  "version": "1.0",
  "description": "Modifies or reads message headers in Thunderbird.",

  "permissions": [
    "messagesRead",
    "accountsRead",
    "compose",
    "background",
    "messageDisplay"
  ],

  "background": {
    "scripts": ["background.js"]
  },

  "messageDisplayAction": {
    "default_icon": "icon.png",
    "default_title": "Header Action",
    "default_popup": "popup.html"
  },

  "browser_specific_settings": {
    "gecko": {
      "id": "youremail@domain.com"
    }
  }
}
```

